---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="description" content="Cloud Coding Agents - The Agentic Era of 2026" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Cloud Coding Agents - The Agentic Era</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="scanline"></div>
    
    <header>
      <div class="subtitle">{'>>>'} WELCOME TO THE</div>
      <h1>CLOUD CODING AGENTS</h1>
      <div class="year">[ THE AGENTIC ERA - 2026 ]</div>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
      <div class="pixel-box">
        <div class="pixel-box-inner">
          <p>
            The <strong style="color: var(--color-pink);">"Agentic Era"</strong> of 2026 has transformed the developer from a coder into an architect. 
            Below is a comprehensive overview of all the cloud-based coding agents, including the high-powered newcomers, Jules and Cursor.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section>
        <h2>[ 1. THE AUTONOMOUS GIANTS ]</h2>
        <p style="margin: 20px 0;">These agents are designed to function as "synthetic employees" that take over entire tickets or features with minimal supervision.</p>

        <div class="agent-card">
          <div class="agent-name">DEVIN</div>
          <div style="color: var(--color-purple-pale); margin: 10px 0;">by Cognition</div>
          <div class="agent-persona">Persona: The "Senior Synthetic Engineer."</div>
          <div class="agent-details">
            <div><span class="agent-label">Execution:</span> Runs in isolated, high-performance cloud VMs with a full browser and terminal.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">Distinction:</span> The industry benchmark for pure autonomy. It can research documentation, find bugs, and fix them without human intervention.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">VCS:</span> Native support for both GitHub and GitLab.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="agent-card">
          <div class="agent-name">FACTORY.AI</div>
          <div style="color: var(--color-purple-pale); margin: 10px 0;">(Droids)</div>
          <div class="agent-persona">Persona: The "Context-Aware Specialist."</div>
          <div class="agent-details">
            <div><span class="agent-label">Execution:</span> Hybrid cloud delegation, allowing for "fire-and-forget" background tasks.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">Distinction:</span> Deep integration with PagerDuty and Slack makes them the best choice for automated incident response ("War Room" mode) and massive repo refactors.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">VCS:</span> Native support for both GitHub and GitLab.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="agent-card">
          <div class="agent-name">OPENHANDS</div>
          <div style="color: var(--color-purple-pale); margin: 10px 0;">(Open Source)</div>
          <div class="agent-persona">Persona: The "Sovereign Agent."</div>
          <div class="agent-details">
            <div><span class="agent-label">Execution:</span> Container-based (Docker/Kubernetes). Can be self-hosted for strict data privacy.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">Distinction:</span> Model-agnostic; you can swap the "brain" (Gemini, Claude, GPT) at any time.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">VCS:</span> Native support for GitHub and GitLab.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>[ 2. THE ECOSYSTEM NATIVES ]</h2>
        <p style="margin: 20px 0;">These agents are vertically integrated into specific cloud or version control platforms for maximum speed and security.</p>

        <div class="agent-card">
          <div class="agent-name">JULES</div>
          <div style="color: var(--color-purple-pale); margin: 10px 0;">by Google Cloud</div>
          <div class="agent-persona">Persona: The "GCP DevOps Companion."</div>
          <div class="agent-details">
            <div><span class="agent-label">Execution:</span> Powered by Gemini 3 Pro in Google Cloud VMs.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">Distinction:</span> Feature-rich for enterprise users, specifically offering Audio Changelogs—an AI voice summary of code changes you can listen to during a commute.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">VCS:</span> Native to GitHub; utilizes Google Cloud bridges for GitLab.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="agent-card">
          <div class="agent-name">GITHUB COPILOT WORKSPACE</div>
          <div class="agent-persona">Persona: The "Mobile Project Manager."</div>
          <div class="agent-details">
            <div><span class="agent-label">Execution:</span> Cloud-native using GitHub Codespaces infrastructure.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">Distinction:</span> The most polished mobile app experience. It allows you to plan, implement, and merge features entirely from your phone via GitHub's native app.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">VCS:</span> GitHub exclusive (No GitLab support).</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="agent-card">
          <div class="agent-name">GITLAB DUO AGENT PLATFORM</div>
          <div class="agent-persona">Persona: The "DevSecOps Specialist."</div>
          <div class="agent-details">
            <div><span class="agent-label">Execution:</span> Runs within GitLab's internal infrastructure.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">Distinction:</span> Focuses on the "Outer Loop"—automatically fixing security vulnerabilities and CI/CD pipeline failures as it codes.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">VCS:</span> GitLab exclusive (No GitHub support).</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="agent-card">
          <div class="agent-name">AWS KIRO</div>
          <div class="agent-persona">Persona: The "Infrastructure-First Agent."</div>
          <div class="agent-details">
            <div><span class="agent-label">Execution:</span> Built on Amazon Bedrock.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">Distinction:</span> Uses "Model Context Protocol" (MCP) to query your live AWS resources directly to ensure code matches your infrastructure.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">VCS:</span> Supports both GitHub and GitLab (via partner bridge).</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>[ 3. THE INTERACTIVE POWERHOUSES ]</h2>
        <p style="margin: 20px 0;">These tools bridge the gap between traditional coding and total autonomy.</p>

        <div class="agent-card">
          <div class="agent-name">CURSOR 2.0</div>
          <div style="color: var(--color-purple-pale); margin: 10px 0;">(Composer Mode)</div>
          <div class="agent-persona">Persona: The "Parallel Orchestrator."</div>
          <div class="agent-details">
            <div><span class="agent-label">Execution:</span> Primarily a desktop IDE, but with a Cloud Agent harness that clones your repo to remote machines for background work.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">Distinction:</span> Its "Composer" interface allows up to 8 agents to work on different parts of your code simultaneously in parallel branches.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">VCS:</span> Deep native support for GitHub and GitLab.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="agent-card">
          <div class="agent-name">REPLIT AGENT</div>
          <div style="color: var(--color-purple-pale); margin: 10px 0;">(Agent 3)</div>
          <div class="agent-persona">Persona: The "Rapid Prototyper."</div>
          <div class="agent-details">
            <div><span class="agent-label">Execution:</span> Entirely browser/cloud-based containers.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">Distinction:</span> The pioneer of "Vibe Coding." You describe an app with voice or text, and it builds, tests, and deploys it instantly. It can even build other "micro-agents" for you.</div>
            <div><span class="agent-label">VCS:</span> Supports imports and syncs for GitHub and GitLab.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>[ 2026 AGENT COMPARISON TABLE ]</h2>
        <div class="comparison-table">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>AGENT</th>
                <th>PRIMARY "BRAIN"</th>
                <th>BEST FOR</th>
                <th>CLOUD CONTROL</th>
                <th>MOBILE STRENGTH</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td style="color: var(--color-pink);">Devin</td>
                <td>Proprietary</td>
                <td>End-to-end tickets</td>
                <td><span class="checkmark">✅</span> Full VM</td>
                <td><span class="stars">⭐⭐⭐⭐</span> (Slack)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="color: var(--color-pink);">Jules</td>
                <td>Gemini 3 Pro</td>
                <td>GCP DevSecOps</td>
                <td><span class="checkmark">✅</span> GCP VM</td>
                <td><span class="stars">⭐⭐⭐⭐</span> (Audio)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="color: var(--color-pink);">Cursor 2.0</td>
                <td>Composer/Multi</td>
                <td>Parallel dev</td>
                <td><span class="checkmark">✅</span> Remote</td>
                <td><span class="stars">⭐⭐</span> (Limited)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="color: var(--color-pink);">Workspace</td>
                <td>GPT-5 / 4o</td>
                <td>Mobile management</td>
                <td><span class="checkmark">✅</span> Codespace</td>
                <td><span class="stars">⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐</span> (App)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="color: var(--color-pink);">Replit</td>
                <td>Agent 3</td>
                <td>Rapid Prototyping</td>
                <td><span class="checkmark">✅</span> Container</td>
                <td><span class="stars">⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐</span> (App)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="color: var(--color-pink);">Factory</td>
                <td>Multi-model</td>
                <td>Incident response</td>
                <td><span class="checkmark">✅</span> Background</td>
                <td><span class="stars">⭐⭐⭐⭐</span> (Slack)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="pixel-box" style="margin-top: 40px; text-align: center;">
        <div class="pixel-box-inner">
          <p style="color: var(--color-cyan);">
            {'>>>'} SELECT YOUR AGENT AND START BUILDING THE FUTURE {'<<<'}
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <footer style="text-align: center; padding: 40px 20px; color: var(--color-purple-bright); border-top: 2px solid var(--color-purple-bright); margin-top: 40px;">
      <div style="font-size: 10px;">
        [ PIXEL PERFECT • RETRO FUTURE • 2026 ]
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
